LZ4 v1.11.1 kernel block-codec tests
==================================

Upstream pin: aa4647fad575d01a874aaaadcdbe8e6a40e072f5 (official v1.11.1).
Frame, file, CLI and threading code are NOT imported or tested here.
The kernel codec uses caller-owned workspaces, not upstream's malloc-owning API.
The historical foundation repair omitted the ARM64 SIMD accelerator. It is now
restored as a separate, reproducible overlay on v1.11.1; see
Documentation/dev-tools/lz4-arm64-restore/README.md. Historical repair receipts
are unchanged. The ARM64 helper exports and first dictionary-free streaming
block can use assembly; generic APIs and dictionary continuations stay C-only.

Prerequisites: native Linux, Clang with its native ASan runtime, make, git,
Python 3, pyelftools and Unicorn (see requirements.txt). The CI entry point uses the
pinned AOSP Clang r614150 snapshot, not GCC and not an arbitrary system Clang.
To use the manual CI test entry point locally, install that complete toolchain
at .toolchains/r614150 with its aosp-prebuilts-commit.txt provenance file:

  bash scripts/ci/test-lz4.sh

This downloads the pinned upstream archive, creates a temporary venv under
out/lz4-tests, verifies all upstream test inputs by SHA-256, and retains test
logs and objects under out/lz4-tests. It does NOT build a bootable image.

For independently obtained, read-only upstream sources and an existing venv:

  python3 -m pip install -r tools/testing/selftests/lz4/requirements.txt
  python3 tools/testing/selftests/lz4/test_codec.py --cc /path/to/clang \
    --asan --ubsan --upstream /path/to/lz4-aa4647fad575d01a874aaaadcdbe8e6a40e072f5
  python3 tools/testing/selftests/lz4/test_build.py --cc /path/to/clang
  python3 tools/testing/selftests/lz4/test_arm64.py --cc /path/to/clang
  python3 tools/testing/selftests/lz4/test_ci.py \
    --anykernel /path/to/clean-pinned-AnyKernel3

--output retains artifacts; otherwise a temporary directory is removed.
--seed changes the upstream unit framework's seed. --compat-upstream optionally
cross-decodes against a separately obtained v1.10.0 tree (also hash checked).
The optional v1.10.0 check was not run for this repair.

Coverage and limitations
------------------------

* test_codec.py compiles the three real kernel codec wrappers separately.
  70 applicable upstream block/HC unit regressions plus four kernel tests
  exercise real STATIC preboot framing, sizes/invalid bounds, poisoned HC
  resets/canaries/levels 1..16, and bidirectional official-upstream decoding.
  The HC test covers the v1.11.1 arbitrary-first-use reset issue and the
  kernel's always-extended 327784-byte state. Levels 13..16 clamp to 12.
* Nine unsupported upstream tests are printed as OMITTED, never counted as
  passes: userspace allocators/obsolete wrappers and the optional small versus
  extended HC-state contract (kernel states always include the scratch).
* Native ASan instrumentation is verified in every codec object; a negative
  signed-overflow probe must trap with UBSan. The independently built upstream
  reference is locally bound (-Bsymbolic), avoiding accidental kernel-symbol
  interposition. Test bridges own allocations outside the codec.
* test_build.py compiles x86-64, i386 and ARM64 freestanding objects with strict
  diagnostics and a 2048-byte frame ceiling; checks static stack usage, ELF
  exports, no duplicate codec symbols or allocator/other-codec dependencies;
  compiles the real preboot include chain for each target; and evaluates all
  27 y/m/n selections in the actual lib/lz4/Makefile. Header shims are minimal
  compile fixtures, NOT a kernel execution environment. The inherited preboot
  wrapper's pointer-sign/unused/sign-compare diagnostics are suppressed only
  for that wrapper, not for the codec object checks.
* test_arm64.py compiles and emulates the repaired donor assembly with strict
  buffer hooks and ABI/x18 checks. Both normal and ThinLTO/SCS/CFI builds run
  483 valid and 1,000 malformed blocks each, both CPU variants, partial decode,
  C-tail history, no-SIMD/no-FPSIMD/DIP/overlap fallbacks and dictionary streaming.
  Feature-off/no-NEON helpers execute as C; STATIC is checked for SIMD references.
  The emulator stubs kernel context primitives; it does not prove their runtime
  behaviour. scripts/ci/test-lz4.sh includes this test in manual CI.
* test_ci.py runs build-script argument/provenance/LLVM-override fixtures and,
  when --anykernel is supplied, the real packager with a clean pinned framework
  and SYNTHETIC NON-BOOTABLE image payloads. It checks ZIP layout/checksum,
  stale-entry removal and rejection cases. These temporary ZIPs are deleted.
  The fixture compiler and make are intentionally fake; this is script-contract
  coverage, not compilation or flash validation. No real source config changes.

None of these tests proves a complete kernel image links, boots, performs
better, or safely flashes. No on-device/stress/performance test is implied.
See Documentation/dev-tools/foundation-repair/README.md for actual results,
real-header Kbuild compilation, source provenance and remaining limits.
